      "created_at": "2026-11-11T12:43:34Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-11T12:44:57Z",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "Hi @fanquake! I'd like to pick this up — could I be assigned?\nI have understood the issue, and here is my approach:\n- `-Werror=dev` is used in `ci/test/03_test_script.sh`, `.github/ci-windows.py`, `.github/ci-test-each-commit-exec.py` and the guix build scripts\n- A plain swap isn't safe: on CMake 3.28, `-Werror=author` is accepted but silently ignored (an `AUTHOR_WARNING` doesn't fail), so the check would be lost below CMake 4.4\n- Fix: choose the flag by CMake version in the CI scripts (`-Werror=author` on ≥ 4.4, `-Werror=dev` otherwise)\n- Leave the guix scripts unless their pinned CMake is ≥ 4.4",
      "user": {
        "login": "AgrimTawani",
        "id": 150522073,
        "node_id": "U_kgDOCPjI2Q",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/150522073?v=4",
